  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-UZB903</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened constituents&apos; capacity to develop and implement gender transformative policies and programmes on gender equality, equal opportunities and treatment in the world of work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO will support the Government in tackling the remaining inequalities and gender gaps in economic and social life in order to improve livelihoods and decent working conditions of women in the world of work. In line with the current Decent Work Country Program Priorities, the ILO&#x2019;s support will include addressing the current gap in provision of affordable and quality care services such as childcare, health and education services, and decent work deficits in the labour market and adequacy of legal provisions and their application to provide for decent work. Through legal assessments, tripartite dialogue and capacity building activities, the ILO will continue to assist the constituents in implementation of the relevant ILO Conventions and ratification of new Conventions including C183 and C190. ILO will continue to provide technical support to the constituents in promoting equal pay for equal work of value, gender-responsive just transition, participatory gender audit, and prevention of discrimination, violence and harassment in the world of. As part of the joint UN efforts on the implementation of the Global Accelerator on Jobs and Social Protection for Just Transition, ILO will continue its policy and technical support on investing in the care economy and protecting rights of care workers including domestic workers.</narrative>
  </description>
